# 🏥 Medical Insurance Charges Prediction

A machine learning project that predicts individual medical insurance costs from age, BMI, smoking status and other factors.

## Overview
Insurance companies need to estimate how much a person's medical cost will be based on their profile. In this project, I built a regression model that predicts `charges` using the **Insurance dataset**. The project covers EDA, encoding, feature engineering, regularization (Ridge/Lasso) and cross-validation, all with Python and scikit-learn.

## Dataset
- **Source:** [Kaggle – Medical Cost Personal Datasets](https://www.kaggle.com/datasets/mirichoi0218/insurance)
- **Size:** 1338 rows, 7 columns

| Feature | Description |
|---|---|
| age | Age of the person |
| sex | Gender (male/female) |
| bmi | Body Mass Index |
| children | Number of dependents |
| smoker | Smoker or not (yes/no) |
| region | Residential region in the US |
| charges | **Target**: medical insurance cost |

## Approach
1. **EDA:** scatter plots (BMI vs charges, coloured by smoker), distributions
2. **Preprocessing:** encoding `sex` and `smoker`, one-hot encoding `region`
3. **Train-test split:** 80% train / 20% test (`random_state=42`)
4. **Model:** Linear Regression (baseline)
5. **Improvements:** scaling, Ridge and Lasso, feature engineering (`bmi × smoker`, `bmi > 30`, `age²`)
6. **Evaluation:** R², Adjusted R², MAE, RMSE and 5-fold cross-validation
7. **Diagnostics:** residual plot and coefficient analysis



## Results
- **Final R²:** 0.7811302113434095
- **Adjusted R²:** 0.7769533069797342


