## Key Insights
- Smoking status is by far the strongest driver of insurance charges.
- The effect of BMI is much larger for smokers than for non-smokers (interaction effect).
- Adding interaction and non-linear features improved the model noticeably over the baseline.
- Scaling did not change plain Linear Regression, but matters for Ridge/Lasso.

